Which CAP properties are followed by Kafka
	•	Kafka is Partition-Tolerant (P)
	•	Can be Consistent (C) or Available (A) depending on producer & topic configuration:
	Config                                 Effect on CAP
    acks=all + min.insync.replicas>1       C + P, may reduce availability under partition
    acks=1 or acks=0                       A + P, may lose consistency during partition
Default Kafka Configuration
	•	Producer acks=1 → The leader writes the message and responds immediately; followers replicate asynchronously.
	•	Replication factor = 1 (by default, if not changed) → No replication unless explicitly configured.
	•	min.insync.replicas = 1 → Only one replica (the leader) is required to acknowledge.
With default settings, Kafka behaves as AP system (Availability + Partition Tolerance):


Which CAP properties are followed by Elasticsearch
By default, Elasticsearch behaves as an AP system (Availability + Partition Tolerance):
CAP Property                                     Behavior
Consistency                                      Eventual (weak consistency)
Availability                                     High (reads/writes possible if at least one shard copy is available)
Partition Tolerance                              Yes (can operate under network partitions)

